  "why": "The statement is the conjecture for every n. KKKMO (2021, Annals 2023) proves it for all sufficiently large n with an unstated threshold, so it is a refereed, digested case and not the whole: a finite range of n remains, and erdosproblems itself calls the problem only 'decidable'. It predates the snapshot. The 2015 claims of a full proof (Lee; Hegde–Dara) are set aside as not credible. Each has several F10 signals: no uptake in a decade on a landmark problem, later papers by top researchers still calling the conjecture open, and in Hegde–Dara's case the authors' own later partial results. Hindman, Romero–Alonso-Pecina and the SAT 2023 work are finite checks (instances). Kahn's (1+o(1))n, Horák–Tuza and Hegde–Dara 2018 are bounds. The codegree t≥2 result, the fractional version, Mubayi–Verstraete and the Berge–Füredi results under extra hypotheses are variants. The post-snapshot items are none or variants: the conditional Berge–Füredi papers, an exposition, a forum label discussion, and a sorry-based Lean file. No event credits any AI system.",
